{"agent_id":"pp3g-TB3o-read-only-plan-sanity-check-do-not-modify-files-do","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T22:15:58.060133884Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"01e136e6-df43-4dc4-a1a5-3f203f1dc3a1","author":"pp3g-TB3o-read-only-plan-sanity-check-do-not-modify-files-do","content":"## [VERDICT] READ-ONLY SANITY-CHECK of the REVISION PLAN (P3-r2) — 2026-08-07\n\nScope: revision-plan review only. No files modified, no commit, no push. #125 NOT closed. Every plan-item citation re-derived from fork@ade6146b (clean tree, HEAD = ade6146b) and from live ASES state.\n\n== HEADLINE ==\n\nEVIDENCE DISCIPLINE: PASS — all 6 items are grounded in reviewer evidence (hy3 17:09/17:25, luna 18:47, big-pickle 18:55) with verifiable file:line references; no item depends on the builder's self-report (the plan explicitly excludes the disproved 'all 3 FAIL' claim and nothing else leaks in).\nSANITY: COHERENT but INCOMPLETE — CHANGES-REQUIRED on the plan. Implementing all 6 as written closes the probe-level wipe routes, but: (1) item 2 cites the permanent-V2-lock-in as evidence yet its stated fix does not address the lock-in chain — needs a scope decision; (2) item 3's explicit caller list omits integrity_cmd.rs:379 (big-pickle MF1's fifth caller); (3) marker-freshness/probe overhead (big-pickle SC7), skip observability (luna SC6), and hydration-entry-point inventory enforcement (luna SC7) are not items; (4) the LIVE TUI wipe hazard is active today (verified: ASES .hub-cache/issues still holds the 4 June-era files; the 12:53 'surgical rm skipped as redundant' reasoning is wrong for the TUI route — the gate covers only maybe_auto_hydrate).\n\n== EVIDENCE DISCIPLINE — all 6 items verified from source ==\n\n| Item | Plan citation | My re-derivation (fork@ade6146b) | Grounded? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 GATE TUI PATHS | tui/mod.rs:534,833 (luna MF2; big-pickle 241->4 live) | tui/mod.rs:534 poll_sync: `let _ = hydrate_to_sqlite(&result.cache_path, &db)` — UNCONDITIONAL, errors swallowed; tui/mod.rs:833 run() startup: `let _ = hydrate_to_sqlite(sync_mgr.cache_path(), db)` — UNCONDITIONAL, no HubMode check, no gate. Live ASES issues/ still has the 4 June-era files (5 entries incl. comments.db) | YES |\n| 2 CLOSE REMOTE-ONLY FAIL-OPEN | hub_v3.rs:732-744 (luna MF1; hy3 live-repro; big-pickle fresh-clone + permanent-V2-lock-in) | hub_is_confidently_v2_only (732-744) calls strict_ref_present (685-714) on the LOCAL repo only (`git rev-parse --verify --quiet` in cache worktree); meta/checkpoint absent locally + v2 branch present => Ok(true). Remote-tracking refs are never probed. detect_remote_hub_version (hub_v3.rs:604-631, `git ls-remote refs/heads/crosslink/*`, Err on spawn/ls-remote failure) already exists — the remote-probe machinery is available | YES (evidence) / PARTIAL (fix scope — see Gap 1) |\n| 3 FIX HubMode-DOWNGRADE PATHS | locks_cmd.rs:303, daemon.rs:279, shared_writer/core.rs:220 (luna MF3; hy3) | locks_cmd.rs:246-247 `if !sync.hub_mode().is_v3() { return sync_v2_readonly(...) }` -> hydrate_to_sqlite at 303. daemon.rs:276-279 `if sync.hub_mode().is_v3() { hydrate_v3_tick } else { hydrate_to_sqlite }`. shared_writer/core.rs:204-220 `if self.is_v3() { ...; return }` else hydrate_to_sqlite at 220/227. HubMode::resolve degrade-to-V2 on detection error confirmed (hub_v3.rs:785-791). Missing from the citation list: integrity_cmd.rs:379 (see Gap 2) | YES (partially incomplete list) |\n| 4 DISCRIMINATING TESTS | hy3 mutation matrix; luna MF4 | Verified by reading the committed tests: test (b) test_maybe_auto_hydrate_still_runs_on_v2_only_hub (hydration.rs:2399-2415) asserts hydration RAN — with the gate removed the v2 path runs and the assert still passes => positive-by-construction (the 11:54 'all 3 FAIL with gate removed' claim is false for (b), as hy3 showed). Test (c) test_maybe_auto_hydrate_fail_closed_on_detection_error (2418-2456) creates BOTH markers and corrupts only meta — checkpoint remains valid, so lenient detection (broken ref collapsed to absent, checkpoint present => V3) ALSO skips => does not discriminate strict_ref_present. hy3's discriminating fixture (broken meta + checkpoint ABSENT + v2 present: strict skips, lenient runs) is correct and not committed | YES |\n| 5 TOCTOU | luna SC5; big-pickle probe-vs-fetch TOCTOU | hydration.rs:1199-1247: marker read (1199-1206), gate probes (1219-1236), hydrate_to_sqlite (1244), marker write (1247) are separate, unlocked operations. acquire_hub_lock exists (sync/cache.rs:56) and fetch() already holds it (cache.rs:300-302) — serialization primitive available | YES |\n| 6 DOCS CORRECTION | big-pickle new finding | Verified live: Addendum 04 'root cause RESOLVED 2026-08-06' (lines 12, 45, 77, 103, 229); crosslink-fork.md 'Root cause fixed 2026-08-06' (line 60); playbook §6.5 'Durable root-cause fix (2026-08-06)' (line 440) — all overstate while the TUI/degrade/fresh-env routes remain | YES |\n\nNo plan item depends on builder self-report. EVIDENCE DISCIPLINE: PASS.\n\n== WIPE-ROUTE CLOSURE (would all 6 close the wipe routes?) ==\n\n| Route (reviewer source) | Plan coverage | Closed by all 6? |\n|---|---|---|\n| maybe_auto_hydrate v2 path (hydration.rs:1244) | Fixed by ade6146b (kept) | YES (already) |\n| TUI startup + 30s poll (tui/mod.rs:833, 534) | Item 1 | YES |\n| locks_cmd.rs:303 (incl. fresh-clone sync_v2_readonly), daemon.rs:279, shared_writer/core.rs:220 (degrade-to-V2) | Item 3 | YES |\n| integrity_cmd.rs:379 (clear_shared_data + hydrate_to_sqlite when v3_state None) | NOT cited explicitly; only via 'every v2 hydration entry point' phrase | ONLY if the implementer inventories it — must be made explicit (Gap 2) |\n| Remote-only-v3-marker probe fail-open (fresh env) | Item 2 | YES (probe-level) |\n| Permanent-V2-lock-in (fresh env: SyncManager caches V2 at construction sync/core.rs:67-70; init_cache v2-first cache.rs:175-185 never reaches fetch_v3_refs_for_join; fetch dispatches V2->fetch_v2_readonly cache.rs:298-320; sync_v2_readonly wipes) | Item 2 cites it as EVIDENCE; no fix/scope decision for the lock-in itself | NO — with items 2+3 the fresh clone becomes stale-but-safe (fail-closed, no data loss), but it never joins v3: sync yields the 4-issue baseline forever. Must be scoped (Gap 1) |\n\n== GAPS — must add to the revision ==\n\nG1. PERMANENT-V2-LOCK-IN SCOPE (big-pickle A4/MF2). Item 2 fixes the probe; the lock-in chain needs an explicit decision: (a) add the v3-join fix (init_cache should join a v3 remote even when a retained v2 branch exists — detect_remote_hub_version already exists, hub_v3.rs:604-631; and/or re-resolve hub_mode after init_cache; and/or delete the remote v2 branch post-migration), or (b) explicitly scope it out and state the outcome is fail-closed-but-stale (fresh clones serve stale data, no wipe). Currently silent.\n\nG2. integrity_cmd.rs:379 (big-pickle MF1 fifth caller). Add to item 3's explicit list. Semantics: on a v3 hub where v3_state fails to resolve, the repair must refuse rather than clear_shared_data + hydrate_to_sqlite from stale v2 files. Also classify the legitimately-v2-only/exempt callers in the inventory: migrate.rs:262 (v2-only import command) and integrity_drift.rs:191 (temp-DB hydration — not destructive to the main DB, but on a v3 hub with stale files it yields a wrong drift view).\n\nG3. MARKER FRESHNESS / PROBE OVERHEAD (big-pickle SC7). Not in the plan. On the gate-skip path .last-hydrated-ref is never refreshed, so every v2-branch tip move (trust/agent/swarm churn — accepted out-of-scope) re-triggers the 3-subprocess probe on every command until the next explicit sync. Either write current_ref on the skip path or explicitly accept the overhead. Cheap, distinct from item 5's TOCTOU.\n\nG4. FAIL-CLOSED SKIP OBSERVABILITY (luna SC6). The skip is a silent debug log (hydration.rs:1228-1234) — stale SQLite indefinitely with no user-visible warning and no documented recovery path. Add an observable warning/metric + state that fail-closed means availability degradation and the recovery is `crosslink sync`.\n\nG5. ENTRY-POINT INVENTORY ENFORCEMENT (luna SC7). The acceptance 'no v2 hydration entry point ungated' is not mechanically verifiable. Add a test that asserts no direct hydrate_to_sqlite callers exist outside the fail-closed dispatcher + the explicit exemptions (G2). Turns comments into an invariant.\n\nG6. INTERIM CONTROL FOR THE LIVE TUI HAZARD (big-pickle A5; verified live). The 12:53 'surgical rm skipped as redundant' reasoning covers only maybe_auto_hydrate — the gate does NOT cover the TUI route. Live state: ASES .hub-cache/issues still holds the 4 June-era files (5 entries incl. comments.db). A user running `crosslink tui` in the ASES main repo wipes the DB today (241->4, timer-driven 30s). Apply the surgical rm (rm -rf .crosslink/.hub-cache/issues) NOW as an interim control — it neutralizes both routes in the v3 main repo (hydrate_to_sqlite early-returns on missing dir, hydration.rs:126-128; v3 fetch never resets the worktree) — and/or warn users off `crosslink tui` until item 1 lands.\n\nG7. BINARY-VS-COMMIT VERIFICATION (big-pickle A1). The 11:47 binary was built from a DIRTY tree at the PARENT sha (0.9.0-beta.1+4efd9ae6-dirty); commit ade6146b came ~6 min later. The r2 verification must confirm the rebuilt binary reports the r2 commit sha so the live-tested artifact matches the committed tree.\n\nNITs: (a) item 1's 'route through v3 hydrate_from_state' needs the TUI's v3 hydration source defined — hydrate_from_state requires a CheckpointState; the dispatcher must specify reduce-on-poll semantics or reuse the sync_cmd path (note the cost: reduce per 30s poll); (b) old-style v3 refs (refs/crosslink/{meta,checkpoint} without /heads/) are not probed (big-pickle NIT 10) — keep the remote probe consistent with classify_hub_version; (c) the docs correction (item 6) should land WITH the code — the current RESOLVED claims are actively misleading while the TUI wipe is live.\n\n== BOTTOM LINE ==\n\nPLAN VERDICT: CHANGES-REQUIRED (on the plan; #125 stays OPEN). Evidence discipline is clean — every item is reviewer-grounded with verified file:line; keep all 6. Before dispatching the builder, add: G1 (lock-in scope decision), G2 (integrity_cmd.rs:379 + exemption classification), G3 (marker freshness/probe overhead), G4 (skip observability), G5 (inventory enforcement test), G6 (apply surgical rm NOW as interim TUI control), G7 (binary sha check in acceptance). Ordering is sound (live wipe routes first); item 4's tests should be written per-fix alongside 1-3, matching the 'tests fail without each fix' acceptance.","created_at":"2026-08-07T22:15:58.052793124Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:cXVGeEHs/KUxAe3pdHRIX1/MJK1j26wr2kKRCF9GvKM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgvI/TYJ1DJ5pnytMDJhhauDerJEy4gLkYHOXtGoT2wZwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA38TawZgM/Gu4diaKF9r8sljPSkIFw4wXKF2z+lo3zR+JDvNHrrjf32M13Rkjn9/rLJMFRNNjys9sKKJfT07tCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:cXVGeEHs/KUxAe3pdHRIX1/MJK1j26wr2kKRCF9GvKM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgvI/TYJ1DJ5pnytMDJhhauDerJEy4gLkYHOXtGoT2wZwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB4VVCB+bJICtSPIamJG0fA+YBhjHrqA+Zzlqmcu+2OkpYatvKwxdzd9AV+V4dvBJ3P6B1or/VzxQky/NzPRjAA="}
